<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="correction" xml:lang="EN"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Int J Clin Pract</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">ijcp</journal-id><journal-title>International Journal of Clinical Practice</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1368-5031</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1742-1241</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Blackwell Publishing Ltd</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2253718</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1742-1241.2007.01357.x</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Erratum</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Errata</article-title></title-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>4</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><volume>61</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>711</fpage><lpage>712</lpage><copyright-statement>&#x000a9; 2007 The Authors Journal compilation &#x000a9; 2007 Blackwell Publishing Ltd</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2007</copyright-year><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="60" page="1364" id="N0x1cea3f0N0x1e1ba40" ext-link-type="pmc"/></article-meta></front><body><p>Original paper &#x02018;Lercanidipine is an effective and well tolerated antihypertensive drug regardless the cardiovascular risk profile: the LAURA study&#x02019;. <italic>Int J Clin Pract</italic> 2006; <bold>60</bold>: 1364&#x02013;70.</p><p>Since publication, an error has been spotted in <xref ref-type="table" rid="tbl1">table 2</xref> which meant that the percentage symbol was excluded. The corrected table is detailed below.</p><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Characteristics of the study population at baseline (<italic>n</italic> = 3175)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Variables</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" colspan="2" rowspan="1"><bold>Biodemographic data</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Sex (male/female) (%)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M: 49 F: 51</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Age (years), mean &#x000b1; SD</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">63&#x000b1;10</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;BMI (kg/m<sup>2</sup>), mean &#x000b1; SD</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M: 28.2&#x000b1;3.8 F: 28.3&#x000b1;4.2</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Waist circumference (cm), mean &#x000b1; SD</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M: 101.3 &#x000b1; 12.2 F: 96.8&#x000b1;14.1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="2" rowspan="1"><bold>Cardiovascular risk factors (%)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Grade I hypertension</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">43</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Grade II hypertension</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">57</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Hypercholesterolemia</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Current smoking</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Family history cardiovascular disease</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Diabetes mellitus</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">15</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="2" rowspan="1"><bold>Target organ damage (%)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Left ventricular hypertrophy</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Atherosclerotic plaques</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Mild renal impairment/microalbuminuria</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="2" rowspan="1"><bold>Associated clinical conditions (%)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Ischaemic heart disease</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Peripheral arterial disease</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Congestive heart failure</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Renal failure</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Cerebrovascular disease</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Advanced retinopathy</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="2" rowspan="1"><bold>Cardiovascular risk (%)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Low risk</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.5</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Medium risk</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">44</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;High</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Very high</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.8</td></tr><tr><td align="left" colspan="2" rowspan="1"><bold>Clinical data (mean &#x000b1; SD)</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;SBP (mmHg)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">159.5 &#x000b1; 11.7</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;DBP (mmHg)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">95.2 &#x000b1; 7.4</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;&#x02003;Heart rate (bpm)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">68.4 &#x000b1; 4.2</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>M, male; F, female; BMI, body mass index; SBP, systolic blood pressure; DPB, diastolic blood pressure.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></body><back><ref-list><title>Reference</title><ref id="b1"><label>1</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barrios</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lercanidipine is an effective and well tolerated antihypertensive drug regardless the cardiovascular risk profile: the LAURA study&#x02019;</article-title><source>Int J Clin Pract</source><year>2006</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>1364</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17073834</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>